Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btqca: patch the WCN3950's NVM baud rate in the right byte

qca_tlv_check_data() writes the UART rate the host asks for into the
NVM's HCI transport tag (17): into its second byte for the WCN3991 and
later, into its third byte for the older chips. The WCN3950 sits before
the WCN3991 in enum qca_btsoc_type, so it gets the third byte, but its
NVM files have the WCN3991's layout of that tag:

  cmnv12.bin, cmnv13*.bin, crnv32*.bin:  15 11 22 00 2e 00
  crnv21.bin, apnv10.bin:                82 01 11 08 04 0a 28 00 15

The byte that holds the rate (0x11 = QCA_BAUDRATE_3200000 by default)
stays as it is, and the one after it is overwritten. With max-speed =
<3200000> the two agree by chance. With any other speed the controller
takes over 3.2 Mbaud from the NVM when the host resets it after the
download, while the host stays at max-speed, and setup fails every time:

  Bluetooth: hci0: QCA Downloading qca/cmnv12.bin
  Bluetooth: hci0: Frame reassembly failed (-84)
  Bluetooth: hci0: command 0x0c03 tx timeout
  Bluetooth: hci0: QCA Reset failed (-110)

Seen on the F(x)tec Pro1X (WCN3950, SoC version 0x40070120, ROM 0x0102)
with max-speed = <3000000>; 3.2 Mbaud worked before.

Write the rate into the second byte for the WCN3950 as well.

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
index dda7636572..c0cb901060 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
@@ -442,8 +442,12 @@ static int qca_tlv_check_data(struct hci_dev *hdev,
 				 */
 				tlv_nvm->data[0] |= 0x80;
 
-				/* UART Baud Rate */
-				if (soc_type >= QCA_WCN3991)
+				/* UART Baud Rate. The WCN3950's NVM files
+				 * (cmnv*.bin) have the 6-byte layout of this
+				 * tag that the WCN3991 uses, with the rate in
+				 * its second byte.
+				 */
+				if (soc_type == QCA_WCN3950 || soc_type >= QCA_WCN3991)
 					tlv_nvm->data[1] = nvm_baud_rate;
 				else
 					tlv_nvm->data[2] = nvm_baud_rate;
